[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one hits a boundary I need your confirmation on before writing anything.

  [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes[39m is irreversible: once the deploy job applies it, the [38;5;153mnotes[39m values for all 48,000
  production rows are gone. There's no rollback — a down-migration can re-add an empty column, but not the data. "We
  stopped using it" is the part I can't verify from the repo; nothing here tells me whether anything still reads [38;5;153mnotes[39m
  or whether the contents are worth keeping.

  Two things I'd want a yes on:

  1. [1mConfirm the data is disposable[0m — no export/backup wanted first, and nothing outside this repo still reads the
     column.
  2. [1mConfirm the drop, not a soft deprecation[0m — the alternative is leaving the column in place and stopping writes to
     it, which is reversible.

  If you say go, the change is small and I'll keep it that way: [38;5;153mmigrations/003_drop_notes.sql[39m with the single [38;5;153mALTER [39m
  [38;5;153mTABLE users DROP COLUMN notes;[39m, plus removing the [38;5;153mnotes[39m line from [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m since the README says that file mirrors
  the migrations by hand.

